WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.406
The identity-maintenance draft lists the

2
00:00:02.406 --> 00:00:04.896
fixes that still happen
once HR is the source.

3
00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:08.817
Here's how the first five land on these
products, mostly as our inference.

4
00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:11.880
A wrong fact in HR goes to
HR as a ServiceNow case;

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.139
HR corrects it in Core HCM, and SailPoint
picks it up on the next aggregation.

6
00:00:17.139 --> 00:00:21.009
A late personnel action, or an
urgent leaver HR hasn't entered,

7
00:00:21.009 --> 00:00:24.833
runs the leaver sequence through
a ServiceNow emergency change.

8
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:29.395
A record the pipeline couldn't apply is
re-run through SailPoint, never by hand.

9
00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:32.527
And the standout is a write
made outside the pipeline.

10
00:00:32.527 --> 00:00:36.902
SailPoint's native change detection catches
it, and SailPoint restores the value.

11
00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.394
That's the closest one-to-one
fit in the catalog.

12
00:00:39.394 --> 00:00:40.440
Here are the rest.
